  "notes": "THE 'STATUTORY' FIXTURE, and the one that lives in kb-samples/endorsements/ rather than certificates/ (specs/03 §15 says so in as many words; it is the off-by-one the old '16 real + 5 synthetic' header had absorbed). Five pages: the State of Nevada's example certificate on page 1, the reverse-side IMPORTANT / DISCLAIMER notices on page 2, an annotated blank certificate on page 3, a sample additional-insured endorsement on page 4 and CG 20 26 11 85 on page 5. Pages 2-4 are scans with no text layer at all. THE EDITION IS 'ACORD 25-S(3/93)' — older than every edition in the schema's enum, and it shows: the form has no ADDL INSD or SUBR WVD columns at all (so those fields are null on every row and this document contributes none of them to the critical-field denominator), it still has GARAGE LIABILITY and FIRE DAMAGE boxes, and its left-hand column is 'CO Ltr' carrying an X rather than an insurer letter. form_edition is therefore 'unknown', which is the honest answer: 'unknown' means 'not one of the four we know', not 'we could not read the footer'. THE WORKERS' COMPENSATION LIMIT BOX PRINTS 'STATUTORY LIMITS' with the tick beside it, so its amount is null with the printed characters in raw — the same rule that stops 'Excluded' becoming $0 on G2. ONE LIMIT IS PRINTED WRONG AND IS LABELLED AS UNREADABLE-AS-A-NUMBER: PRODUCTS – COMP/OP AGG reads '$1,000.000', with a comma and a full stop. Read strictly it is one thousand; read as the typo it obviously is, one million. A labeller may not guess between them, so amount.value is null and raw keeps '$1,000.000'. The document is riddled with the same class of error ('CONVERS', 'OCCURANCE', 'SAFFORDED', 'NMAE', 'ENDEAVER', '© ACCORD CORPORATION'), which is what makes this the right document to be strict on. The cyan callout boxes ('MINIMAL', 'ANY AUTO SHOULD BE COVERED', 'If worker's comp is required...', 'THIS STATEMENT SHOULD DESCRIBE CONTRACT AND INCLUDE ADTL INSURED') are annotations and are not labelled.",
